    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nWhen an owner is created (or fetched), the API now returns a `displayName` field formatted exactly as `LastName, FirstName` from the stored names.\n\nTwo changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` response schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct mapping that computes it from the entity:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"displayName\", expression = \"java(owner.getLastName() + \\\", \\\" + owner.getFirstName())\")\n   OwnerDto toOwnerDto(Owner owner);\n   ```\n\nBecause both the create (`POST /api/owners`) and read (`GET /api/owners/{id}`) responses go through `toOwnerDto`, the computed value is consistent across both endpoints. The acceptance test `coreComputesDisplayName` and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).",
